              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "If you're in the market for a dry van trailer, chances are you're thinking beyond the purchase price. You're thinking about cash flow, long-term value, and how this decision impacts your business. That's where dry van trailer financing comes in. Instead of tying up capital in a full purchase, financing gives you the flexibility to get the equipment you need now while keeping your business moving forward.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "For owner-operators and fleet managers alike, it's often the difference between waiting and growing. At <a href=\"/locations/trailer-sales\">Sun State Trailers</a>, financing isn't treated like a side option. It's part of helping you make a practical, well-informed decision that supports your operation long-term.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-why-finance",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Why Financing a Dry Van Trailer Makes Sense",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "why-finance"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-finance-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "There's a reason more businesses are turning to dry van trailer finance options instead of paying up front. Here's how your business can benefit:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "features-why-finance-2",
                  "type": "list",
                  "props": {
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "columns": 3,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "label": "Preserve Cash Flow",
                        "desc": "Running a trucking business means constant expenses: fuel, maintenance, and payroll. Financing a dry van trailer allows you to keep cash on hand for those day-to-day needs."
                      },
                      {
                        "label": "Scale at the Right Time",
                        "desc": "When demand picks up, waiting to save for a full purchase can cost you opportunities. Financing helps you grow your fleet when your business needs it, not months later."
                      },
                      {
                        "label": "Predictable Payments",
                        "desc": "With structured financing, you know exactly what to expect each month. That kind of consistency makes it easier to plan and manage your business."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "fig-1",
                  "type": "image",
                  "props": {
                    "width": "full",
                    "image": {
                      "src": "/img/blog/dry-van-trailer-financing-at-sun-state-trailers/1.jpg",
                      "width": 1000,
                      "height": 667,
                      "alt": "Sun State technician checking a dry van trailer's rear door hardware and locking mechanism"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-options",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Understanding Your Dry Van Trailer Financing Options",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "options"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-options-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Not all dry van trailer financing options are created equal. The right choice depends on your business goals, budget, and how you plan to use the trailer.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "cards-options-2",
                  "type": "card-lists",
                  "props": {
                    "variant": "option",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "title": "Equipment Financing",
                        "points": [
                          {
                            "text": "Long-term ownership"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Businesses planning to keep trailers for years"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Owner-operators building equity in their equipment"
                          }
                        ],
                        "intro": "This is the most common option. You finance the trailer itself, make monthly payments, and own it at the end of the term.",
                        "lead": "BEST FOR"
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Lease-to-Own",
                        "points": [
                          {
                            "text": "Businesses that want lower upfront costs"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Operators testing growth before committing fully"
                          }
                        ],
                        "intro": "This structure gives you flexibility. You make payments like a lease, but with the option to own the trailer at the end.",
                        "lead": "BEST FOR"
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Traditional Leasing",
                        "points": [
                          {
                            "text": "Seasonal demand"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Short-term contracts"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Businesses that rotate equipment frequently"
                          }
                        ],
                        "intro": "If you're focused on short-term flexibility, leasing may be the better fit. You use the trailer without committing to full ownership.",
                        "lead": "BEST FOR"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-options-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "The key is working with a team that helps you understand what fits, not just what's available.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
